' for main)","search of src/rebar/mirror_guard.py for 'refs/changes' returns (no matches) — the guard never samples change refs","Plan text: 'Watch the first Mirror Guard run after the change and confirm it stays green with no replication-lag alarm.' — but the named problem is a MISSING refs/changes/* ref, which Mirror Guard does not observe","The g2p checkout-gerrit-change-action fetches refs/changes/NN/NNNN/P, not main — the failure class Mirror Guard watches is orthogonal to the change refs this ticket publishes"],"finding":"The plan's post-change verification / AC ties success to 'Mirror Guard remains green after the change and no replication-lag alarm is observed', but Mirror Guard only checks Gerrit-vs-GitHub `main` SHA divergence and has no refs/changes/* coverage, so it cannot confirm the fix actually converged the change-ref namespace.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f33346e5c9a34bd95","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan > Plan (last bullet) and Acceptance Criteria (final item)","norm_id":"nab494af3120bcc8f","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Change-ref replication silently lags or a subset of refs/changes/* fail to push, yet Mirror Guard stays green because `main` is in sync — the operator concludes the fix succeeded while CI checkouts could still fall back to Gerrit"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reframe the final AC around the operational refs/changes/* verification (ls-remote + fetch-from-GitHub-only) as the pass signal for the fix, and state that Mirror Guard is used only to confirm the unchanged main/tag one-way-door was not disturbed — not to verify change-ref replication (which it does not observe).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"n